.TH geectl-request-list 1  "geectl-request-list 0.2.4" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-request\-list \- List submit requests: the same search, with the states still awaiting action (new, review) as the default. A thin wrapper over the search operation: the flags select the same server\-side search
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl request list\fR [\fB\-\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-package\fR] [\fB\-\-state\fR] [\fB\-\-since\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
List submit requests: the same search, with the states still awaiting action (new, review) as the default. A thin wrapper over the search operation: the flags select the same server\-side search
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fI<PROJECT>\fR
Requests touching this project
.TP
\fB\-\-package\fR \fI<PACKAGE>\fR
Requests touching this package; requires `\-\-project`
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fI<STATE>\fR
Requests in this state; when empty, new and review
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fI<SINCE>\fR
Only requests with a history entry at or after this date, or a last update at or after it, as `YYYY\-MM\-DD` or `YYYY\-MM\-DDTHH:MM:SS`
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR
Ask the server for at most this many matches
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH VERSION
v0.2.4
